from collections import defaultdict
H,W=20,13
bg=4
G=[[bg]*W for _ in range(H)]
pat=[[4,5,5],[8,5,8],[8,5,0]]
sr,sc=11,6
for i in range(3):
  for j in range(3): G[sr+i][sc+j]=pat[i][j]
marks=[(1,2),(1,9),(6,11),(7,4),(12,2),(13,11),(17,4),(17,8)]
# Stamp only non-bg cells; report full intended locations, overlaps, and output.
changes=defaultdict(list); overlaps=[]
for r,c in marks:
  for i in range(3):
    for j in range(3):
      rr,cc=r+i-1,c+j-1
      if not (0<=rr<H and 0<=cc<W): raise ValueError((rr,cc))
      val=pat[i][j]
      if val!=bg:
        if G[rr][cc]!=bg: overlaps.append(((rr,cc),G[rr][cc],val,(r,c)))
        G[rr][cc]=val
        changes[(rr,cc)].append(val)
print('overlaps:', overlaps)
print('changed cells:',len(changes))
for rr,row in enumerate(G): print(' '.join(map(str,row)))
print('stamp centers:',marks)
print('stamp boxes:',[(r-1,r+1,c-1,c+1) for r,c in marks])
# Compare transparent vs opaque stamps from same input.
G2=[[bg]*W for _ in range(H)]
for i in range(3):
  for j in range(3): G2[sr+i][sc+j]=pat[i][j]
